{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Variable parts",
  "exampleId": "block-variable-parts",
  "description": "The variable resistor swings between 5 Ω and 15 Ω on 10 V, so its current is 10/R: 0.67 A at 0.25 s and 2 A at 0.75 s. The inductor on 1 V builds flux linkage t, so its current is t/L: 1/3 A at 1 s, when L = 3 H, and 1 A at 2 s, when L = 2 H. The capacitor charges at 1 mA; when its capacitance doubles at 0.5 s its charge stays, so its voltage halves. The potentiometer wiper sweeps from 0 V to 10 V as the position input goes from 0 to 1.",
  "duration": 2,
  "revision": 0,
  "blocks": [
